A||||7||Formula||cracked head????||||1||
Z||000000||Formula||03-19-2000||02:09 PM||||the guy who sold me my GT said that it had a cracked head. <P>visually:<P>1. no water in the oil<P>2. after idling for 30 mins, the motor didnt overheat.  It was out of antifreeze when I got it though.<P>3. It only smokes white at startup, and it smokes whne you hit the gas hard in the first 30 mins, then it doesnt smoke.<P>4. It seems weird that a iron head would crack.<P>5. It idles faster then my formula.<P>6. It stalls if I hold the clutch in after startup for more then 10 secs.<P>7. THERE IS NO THERMOSTAT, would this make someone think it was a cracked head because the CAR WOULD OVERHEAT.<P>8. it has a performance chip.  just thought I would say that.<P>9. Im trying to get 10.<P>10. ok<P>______________<P>How would my car be acting if I had a cracked head, and have you ever had a cracked head on the 2.8?<P>The cradle needs dropped anyway for a clutch/flyweel job, so I might just need a new motor for it.  but, it isn't a daily driver so if the heads are ok I will build it into a 3.1.  <P>Oh yeah, would the 2.8/4 speed accelerate a lot faster then the 2.8 auto?||||reg||1
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||03-19-2000||03:00 PM||||2. The motor didn't overheat because there is no thermostat.<P>3. Smoking at startup means the heads may be worn, not cracked... normal for a high mileage motor.<P>5. It may be ideling high beacause the thermostat is missing and the motor is in open-loop.<P>7. A missing thermostat won't make it over-heat... just the opposite. It lets all the water through as soon as you start the car. It needs to limit the flow of water until the motor reaches normal operating temperature.<P>10 lol...<P>I would get a thermostat in that thing then run it to warm it up and do a pressure test on the cooling system. Autozone and Checker will rent you one for free(give deposit and get it back when you bring the tester back in). This is the easiest way to tell if there is a crack anywhere in the cooling system. <P>As far as the 2.8/4spd accelerating faster than an auto. I think the manual is much faster then the auto.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||03-19-2000||07:39 PM||||The word "fast" can not be used in the same sentence as "automatic". Pleasant might be a better choice.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||03-20-2000||05:43 PM||||My auto is fast DAMNIT||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GT||03-20-2000||06:05 PM||||When I bought my fiero, the previous owner had the thermostat out because he had the hypertech chip in it and he was suppose to do that.  I left the chip in but put the thermostat back in hoping it would run a little smoother and warm up quicker.  Well it didnt affect the performance and the car heats up very well.  IT has high idle when cold(1500) but after about 10 minutes its down to 900.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||william_thorniii||03-20-2000||07:07 PM||||The fast idle is probably a cracked EGR tube or similar vacuum leak.  It sounds to me like the previous owner was not truly aware of the car's problems.  That is why I would try to look into other possible causes of the fast idle.  What I would reccomend is to get a spray bottle filled with (preferrably a non-flammable) liquid.  Spray in concentrated areas around your engine bay.  If the idle changes when you spray one certain area, you have found your leak.  <P>Hope this helps,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000006||Formula||03-20-2000||09:02 PM||||Thanks, I'll try these on Saturday and give a report.  Just working on one fiero every weekend wasnt enough for me. lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||batboy||03-20-2000||10:47 PM||||Actually, cast iron head crack fairly frequently, maybe not as much as aluminum heads, but often enough. A cracked head will often cause an engine to overheat. But, with a Fiero, if they ran it low on coolant or got air into the system, it might of started overheating and they just thought it was a cracked head. Slap a thermostat back into it, they pulled that out when it started overheating in case it was stuck closed. Do a compression check. Check for coolant leaks. I wonder how hot the ol' motor got and for how long? Probably multiple problems. A real light blue smoke (maybe looks white to you?) on start up is common with a high mileage engine.||||reg||1
